WEBVTT

00:00:01.940 --> 00:00:06.291
So in the previous video
we looked at destroying

00:00:06.303 --> 00:00:11.678
the objects when we clinked at them, but in
this case we wanted to be able to destroy

00:00:11.690 --> 00:00:13.400
the targets if they
collide with a specific

00:00:13.401 --> 00:00:19.480
sensor and we're going to have a trigger
at the very bottom of this play area.

00:00:19.481 --> 00:00:23.293
I'm going to right-click
my hierarchy, choose

00:00:23.305 --> 00:00:26.960
3D object and just
choose A, choose a cube.

00:00:26.961 --> 00:00:33.200
Now once I've got that I'm just going to
move it down here and I'm just going to scale

00:00:33.201 --> 00:00:38.520
it out across this portion so you know
you can see our cube in the scene view.

00:00:38.521 --> 00:00:42.200
We want to make sure that it's got a box
collider and it's set to its trigger and then

00:00:42.201 --> 00:00:44.560
we're going to need to
make sure that it has a tag.

00:00:44.561 --> 00:00:48.560
We'll add a brand new tag, so once we're
there in the tags we'll add the little plus

00:00:48.561 --> 00:00:51.208
box, we'll just call
this tag it destroys on

00:00:51.220 --> 00:00:53.760
but leave it together
without a space just

00:00:53.761 --> 00:00:59.080
so that it can reference nicely in code,
we'll click Save, we'll go back to our cube

00:00:59.081 --> 00:01:05.000
and I'm going to set that cube and set that
to the name of destroys on and then we'll

00:01:05.001 --> 00:01:10.360
go up to the inspector, go to the
tag and set that to destroys on too.

00:01:10.361 --> 00:01:17.200
If we go into our target script we're
going to create ourselves a new method.

00:01:17.201 --> 00:01:20.773
This can be below our
helper methods here

00:01:20.785 --> 00:01:24.720
and it's going to be a
void on trigger, enter

00:01:24.769 --> 00:01:26.893
so that when one of
our objects collides with

00:01:26.905 --> 00:01:29.040
that danger zone it's
going to destroy itself

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:32.331
so we need an if
statement again, if other

00:01:32.343 --> 00:01:35.960
dot compare tag in
brackets and then in quotes

00:01:37.160 --> 00:01:40.897
is destroy zone then
what we'll do is we'll say

00:01:40.898 --> 00:01:47.480
destroy with a capital
in brackets in object.

00:01:47.481 --> 00:01:53.280
Now when we're back into unity what we can
do is we can test this out and each of our

00:01:53.329 --> 00:01:55.912
prefabs already has
the target script, want

00:01:55.924 --> 00:01:58.640
to make sure that at
least one of the objects

00:01:58.664 --> 00:02:01.081
that collides with a
trigger has a rigid body

00:02:01.093 --> 00:02:03.360
and all of our targets
do, we need to make

00:02:03.361 --> 00:02:06.084
sure that our destroys
on is set to its trigger

00:02:06.096 --> 00:02:08.600
so that when we enter
these it will destroy

00:02:09.260 --> 00:02:12.782
them so now if I hit
play you can see the

00:02:12.794 --> 00:02:16.760
when our objects spawn
they do spawn quite low

00:02:16.761 --> 00:02:20.010
and they do hit our
destroys on which it shows

00:02:20.022 --> 00:02:23.000
that it's working but
for the sake of this

00:02:25.080 --> 00:02:28.977
instance we can either
pull the destroys on

00:02:28.989 --> 00:02:33.080
down so that they will
still spawn over that.

00:02:33.081 --> 00:02:35.443
Now if we just go into
the 3D mode because

00:02:35.455 --> 00:02:40.617
some of the items do interact with each
other we can just make this in scale our our

00:02:40.629 --> 00:02:43.880
destroys on much much
bigger so no matter where

00:02:43.881 --> 00:02:46.801
any of these objects
it do actually fall they

00:02:46.813 --> 00:02:49.680
will always be destroyed
and when we go back

00:02:49.730 --> 00:02:52.566
into 2D mode you will
never actually see it

00:02:52.578 --> 00:02:55.560
so what I want you to
be able to do is create

00:02:55.561 --> 00:02:57.749
a brand new object
by right clicking in the

00:02:57.761 --> 00:03:00.320
hierarchy choosing 3D and
you can choose something

00:03:00.570 --> 00:03:03.436
like cube rename it to
destroy zone make sure

00:03:03.448 --> 00:03:06.200
you give it a tag of
destroy zone make sure

00:03:06.201 --> 00:03:10.360
it's got a box collider set to its trigger
you can scale this out and make sure it's

00:03:10.385 --> 00:03:14.207
below our objects that
spawn in the game world

00:03:14.219 --> 00:03:20.190
and in the 3D mode if you click the little
2D button at the top you can make sure that

00:03:20.202 --> 00:03:22.800
it's big enough just if
some of those objects

00:03:22.801 --> 00:03:28.200
escape or interact when you didn't expect
go inside your target script and towards the

00:03:28.201 --> 00:03:32.640
bottom of the script below the helper methods
will create a brand new void on trigger

00:03:32.641 --> 00:03:35.800
enter if this object
interacts with the object

00:03:35.812 --> 00:03:39.641
destroy zone then we'll just
destroy this particular game object